  "Question": "Two high school classes took the same test. One class of \\(20\\) students made an average grade of \\(80\\%\\); the other class of \\(30\\) students made an average grade of \\(70\\%.\\) The average grade for all students in both classes is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(75\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(74\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(72\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(77\\%\\)",
    "E": "None of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Each student's grade must count once, so the two class averages receive weights equal to their class sizes. Expressing all grades on a \\(100\\)-point scale, the first class has total score \\(20\\cdot80=1600\\), and the second has total score \\(30\\cdot70=2100\\).\n\nThere are \\(20+30=50\\) students, so their combined average is\n\\[\n\\frac{1600+2100}{50}\n=\\frac{3700}{50}=74.\n\\]\nThus the average grade is \\(74\\%\\), choice B.",
